        "original_id": "9b127828-b596-578b-8cff-0a14340f5d98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death\n- People: William Inge, Elia Kazan, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Topics: film production, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he became a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- Splendor in the Grass was written by William Inge, directed by Elia Kazan, and scored by jazz composer David Amram.\n- William Inge briefly appeared in Splendor in the Grass as a Protestant clergyman and won an Oscar for its screenplay.\n- Zohra Lampert, born on May 13, 1937, is an American actress who starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in Splendor in the Grass.\n- In 1971, Zohra Lampert played the title character in the cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death.\n- The New York Times described Elia Kazan as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Elia Kazan died on September 28, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
